# R09 checkpoint package — prepared for Human review

This package reconciles inherited R03–R05 product documents with the public work tree and defines how to record the first backend/Web implementation slice. It does not re-decide approved business rules, accept future outputs, relax any gate, or close R09. Existing21document approval provenance is in docs/kidea-handoff.md; native Android/iOS remain Future without schedule.

The replan proposal preserves the ten original STEP IDs/order and current round. It introduces scoped TODO leaves and stable references; no DONE/executionStatus/resultRefs/gateIds are imported in the proposal. Every original placeholder is explicitly REASSESSed because changing step1 affects downstream planning. Public helpers must record actual progression after the exact package is accepted. Historical checkpoints, failures and source commits remain available. Only public APIs write .kidea.

## Completion definitions

<a id="scope"></a>
### Step1 — scope content
Complete when inherited features/boundaries and current Web-only/lab constraints have been compared to their accepted provenance, with no new requirement silently added. This is content reconciliation, not application execution.

<a id="business"></a>
### Step2 — business content
Complete when the inherited feature/shared-rule/test definitions are bound to the accepted R03 content and Web amendment. The approved max2ACTIVE change remains a later T04 operation; PAUSED cancellation remains a later T09 operation. No runtime case is marked passed by this step.

<a id="quality"></a>
### Step3 — quality targets
Complete when the inherited R04 quality decisions and thresholds are preserved as targets. Actual performance, recovery and reliability verification remains in implementation/release work; accepting target definitions is not proof they have been met.

<a id="experience"></a>
### Step4 — experience/SEO design
Complete when inherited UX1–UX6 and lab noindex policy are reconciled. Keep server-authoritative identity, stable public URLs, readable SSR and explicit unknown state. No public crawl/index or native acceptance.

<a id="operations"></a>
### Step5 — operations design
Complete when inherited signal/alert/response/privacy definitions remain bound to R04. Runtime observer/backup/monitoring is still pending implementation, not inferred from this content gate.

<a id="admin"></a>
### Step6 — admin design
Complete when inherited admin intent/dirty-field/audit/permission design is reconciled. It does not claim the admin UI or operational screens exist.

<a id="architecture"></a>
### Step7 — architecture and profiles
Complete when inherited architecture and current common/C++/Web profiles are reconciled against R04/R05 acceptance. Native profiles retain Future status. Product code and environment tests remain separate evidence.

<a id="technical-tests"></a>
### Step8 — technical test definitions
Complete when inherited137source obligations and20TC groups remain intact as test definitions. They are not137passed application tests. Existing sample/lab results cannot substitute for the new pilot.

<a id="implementation"></a>
### Step9 — implementation, unfinished MVP
Step9 must remain incomplete while any of the following leaves is pending. This is a planning gate; intermediate completion needs actual evidence and final step completion still requires output acceptance.

<a id="backend-leaf"></a>
The backend foundation leaf requires the frozen build-r10 source/artifact and full four-preset evidence, retaining EXr2 and raw failures.

<a id="web-leaf"></a>
The first Web leaf requires33unit,18SSR–Chrome checks and real HTTPS integration on bound backend/Web artifacts, including OPEN/PAUSED and lost-response/history/privacy paths. Its scope excludes admin, live events/ops and final quality/release verification.

<a id="max2-leaf"></a>
Implement the already approved max2ACTIVE change through the public impact workflow while the original MVP remains unfinished. Bind old/new requirements and every affected consumer, preserve prior work and run G2 on final source.

<a id="admin-ops-leaf"></a>
Implement and verify the remaining admin, live events, reconciliation, monitoring and backup obligations from the inherited profiles. No sample PASS substitution.

<a id="g2-leaf"></a>
Run the required whole-project G2 on final source, resolve findings and obtain output acceptance before completing the implementation STEP.

<a id="release"></a>
### Step10 — release and operational confirmation
Prepare an exact fake-data lab release and compatibility/restore scripts before Human performs the approved PROD role. Record each attempt and observation separately; UNKNOWN/FAILED is not deployed. Preserve the requirement to verify running identity, recovery and final quality. No production/cloud deployment is authorized by this package.

<a id="boundaries"></a>
## Retained boundaries

Full R09 execution authority covers technical work/retries within the agreed resource limits. Human output acceptance, review identity/digest, PROD-role action and final R09 acceptance remain distinct. Three-map receipts may contain unresolved calls/dispatch or unfinished consumers; do not label them complete or remove diagnostics for this checkpoint. R10 phase remains unopened. The pilot is local Git/master with no remote.
